// Code signing for the iosApp target.
//
// `DEVELOPMENT_TEAM` is a per-machine value — an Apple developer team ID only works on the Mac
// that holds the matching certificate and private key, so committing one team ID would break the
// build for everyone else. It lives in `Signing.local.xcconfig`, which is gitignored.
//
// After cloning, create that file next to this one:
//
//     DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = XXXXXXXXXX
//
// Find your team ID with:
//
//     security find-certificate -c "Apple Development: <your apple id>" -p \
//       | openssl x509 -noout -subject
//
// and read it out of the `OU=` field. Xcode's Signing & Capabilities tab also writes the value,
// but into the .xcodeproj — put it here instead so the project file stays machine-neutral.
//
// The include is optional (`#include?`), so a clone with no local file still configures and
// builds for the Simulator; only a device build fails, with "requires a development team".
#include? "Signing.local.xcconfig"
